>> title: Alfajores
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: dulce de leche, cornstarch, argentinian, sandwich, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Panadería
>> aka: alfajor, alfajores de maicena, dulce de leche sandwich cookies
>> servings: 24
>> time: 1 hour 30 min

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

Whisk @cornstarch{1 1/2%cup}(190 g), @all-purpose flour{1%cup}(125 g), @baking powder{1%tsp}(4.8 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Cream @unsalted butter{3/4%cup}(170 g; softened) with @powdered sugar{3/4%cup}(90 g).

>> step: beat in
Beat @egg yolks{3}(50 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), and @brandy{1%Tbs}(15 mL; or milk) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

Stir @&(~3)dry ingredients{} into @&(~1)batter{}.

>> step: roll 1/4 in thick, cut rounds, bake 350°F (175°C) 10 min
Roll @&(~1)dough{} 1/4 in thick, cut rounds, and bake at 350°F for ~{10%min}.

>> step: sandwich, roll the edges in coconut
Sandwich @&(~1)cookies{} with @dulce de leche{1%cup}(300 g) and roll the edges in @shredded coconut{1/2%cup}(40 g).
